WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.090
- I don't know about you guys

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.530
but every once in a while,
I'll just have a day

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:06.190
where my brain is actually working well.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.290
The gears of my mind are fully lubricated,

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.160
fully torqued.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.960
When I'm in a conversation with somebody,

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.430
I don't have to search
for the right words to say

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.330
they kinda just bubble up to the surface

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.860
and I can sling them out
of my mouth onto them.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.940
Or if I'm reading a book

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.690
I'm actually able to
comprehend what I'm reading.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.690
I'm actually absorbing the material

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:26.870
or maybe I'm at a party

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.270
and I'm just a little bit more confident.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.150
I have a bit more swagger in my step

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.580
and I'm way more social than I usually am.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.240
If you've had a similar experience

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.470
you probably also know that
these moments are fewer

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.160
and further in between
than we'd probably like.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.200
It almost seems like once in
a while, the universe decides

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.590
to zap us with this extra
level of mental clarity.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.670
It's like a glimpse of our potential,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.530
it's a glimpse of how
social or how confident

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:56.270
or how clear-headed we could
be if we did the right things.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.750
And it was actually this
very feeling that got me

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.960
into self-improvement way
back when I was a teenager,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.510
way back when I was a teenager.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.760
And I was kinda frustrated
that I didn't feel

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.050
like this all the time.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.750
I wanted to get to the bottom of it.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.290
How can I more consistently feel

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.380
like there's not this brain fog?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.210
How do I operate at my
full potential more often?

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.190
Well, I'm happy to report
that I haven't figured it out.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.230
I'm not gonna pretend
like I know the answer

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.070
to living at your full potential

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.650
every single day of the week

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.760
because I don't think
that's actually possible.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.890
It's a little bit of a
fallacy of perfection

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.470
but I wanna go over three things

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.870
that have really helped
me clear mental fog.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.010
And it helps me operate closer

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.850
to my mental potential than
if I didn't do those things.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.920
But right before we jump into these tips

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.970
a word from our, no, I'm
just kidding, not sponsor.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:43.960
That comes later.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.430
I just wanna say that if
you haven't seen my video

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.830
on how to stop being tired all the time,

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.030
I think that is a necessary
precursor to this video

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:54.530
because if you are doing things wrong

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:57.180
in your sleep, diet and exercise,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.880
which are kind of your
fundamentals to feeling well,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.030
then I don't think doing
these additional tips

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.500
will necessarily help you.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.070
But if you do feel like you
have a pretty good grasp

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.170
on your sleep, diet and exercise

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.920
and you're still feeling mentally
sluggish and brain foggy,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.070
and your life's a mess,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.890
then maybe these tips will help you.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.500
So strategy number one
is to practice something

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.470
I like to call graduated stimulation.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.700
From my experience, a
great deal of my lack

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.930
of mental clarity is stimulation-induced.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.710
When I do something
that's overly stimulating

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.870
like browsing social
media for hours and hours

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.680
or I get into a YouTube rabbit hole

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.830
just bingeing videos all day long,

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.600
I sort of start to develop a brain fog.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.550
It might be a result

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.340
of kind of turning your
rational brain off for a while

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.380
and just indulging in
this primal existence

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.700
where you're just injecting yourself

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.490
with dopamine and stimulation
like you're fiend.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.950
And this is a problem because I feel

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.950
like a lot of us have a habit
of doing our internet rounds.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.140
First thing in the morning

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.510
we check Facebook, Twitter,
Instagram, Reddit, YouTube.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.460
We kinda just see what's new in the world

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.300
is sort of giving ourselves
hits of stimulation

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.240
before we've even done anything.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.010
Before we've even fed ourselves,

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.870
before we've cleaned ourselves up.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.540
This makes it extremely difficult to hop

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.070
into something more
boring, more slow-paced

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:25.810
like doing whatever your
job is, writing an essay.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.760
So a way to solve this problem

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.340
is to practice graduated stimulation.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.800
To organize your day

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.380
in a way that sort of
ramps up the stimulation

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.780
as the day goes on.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.440
So say whatever the most
important thing you have to do

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.480
in the day is like one
out of 10 entertaining.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.670
It's not very fun.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:44.810
You're kinda dreading it.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.730
You should do that thing
as soon as possible.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:51.010
When you first wake up, when
you have that mental energy

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.930
before your brain is absolutely corroded,

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.580
you should dive into that one out of 10,

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.950
not very fun thing first.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.320
And then you can move on

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.700
to things that are
gradually more entertaining

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.070
as the day goes on

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.520
and as your willpower
seems to sort of drain

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.440
and your physical energy levels
start to drain, et cetera.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.700
So with this method,

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.290
you're not really cutting
out these internet rounds

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.770
that everyone seems to do.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.010
You don't have to stop really
checking your social media

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.090
but you should postpone that

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.640
until after you've done
the most important things

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.410
that you have to do on your to-do list.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.370
That way it doesn't seem

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.130
like there's such a huge
entertainment disparity

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.650
between your habitual pleasures

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.410
and the things that you
actually have to do.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.090
If you start from zero

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.900
than doing the not so fun
thing is actually more fun

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.470
than doing nothing a lot of the time.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.430
Whereas if you're bingeing social media,

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.330
which is like seven out
of 10 fun for a 10 fun

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.870
and then you try to do the
less stimulating boring thing

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.270
it seems like you're missing out.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.140
It's like, "Oh, this is dreadful."

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.090
I've never used that word

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.610
in a video in my entire life.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.530
Strategy number two is brain dumping.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.270
One of the craziest things

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.990
about the human mind is
that a bare minimum of 90%

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.390
of all of our brain
activity is subconscious.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.630
And I say a bare minimum
because there's a little bit

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:12.500
of argument in the
scientific realm about this.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.390
Some scientists say that this
number is as high as 99.9%.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.630
Of all of our mental function happens

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.070
at the subconscious level,

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.620
which means that as we go about our day,

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.960
everything that we're
in-taking, inputting,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.190
everything that we're smelling,

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.910
we're seeing, we're hearing,

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.260
is being processed behind the scenes

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.760
even though we may not be
consciously aware of it.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.320
This is extremely important

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.260
when it comes to mental clarity

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.980
because we really need to monitor

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.240
what our subconscious knows

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.700
because even though we might
not be paying attention to it,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.340
we still know about it
and it still affects us

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.030
and it leaks into every
single thing that we do.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:53.040
A great example of this is if
you have a business meeting

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.520
or something you're supposed to remember

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.020
maybe an errand or taxes
you're supposed to fill out,

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.550
the more things that you have
piling up that you need to do

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.820
even if you're not paying attention to it,

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.230
the stress of these things

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.030
is going to affect every
aspect of your being.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.650
By putting things off,
by postponing things,

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.520
by procrastinating things,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.270
we're pretty much delegating it

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.240
to our subconscious to worry about.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.820
And if we delegate too many things

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.580
to our subconscious to worry about,

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.190
it can often start to become way too much.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.480
And it starts to...

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.900
we start to become anxious

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.460
and stressed and
overloaded and brain foggy.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:31.270
So I think a great way
to deal with this problem

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:34.010
and make sure that you
greatly reduce the risk

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:36.110
of this happening is
by getting in the habit

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.840
of doing something that I
like to call a brain dump.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.180
Every single possible little thing,

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.450
everything you have to do,

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.490
everything you're responsible for,

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.550
everything that you need to remember,

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.600
you write down.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.440
You have a giant document
where you just let loose.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.900
And it may seem counterproductive

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:54.860
to have a giant mountainous list of things

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:55.830
that you have to do.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.380
You might feel like you will
get overwhelmed with this.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.630
In my experience, it's
a lot less stressful

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:04.320
to have this giant list than
to have that list in your head

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.570
leaking into every
single thing that you do

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.403
throughout the day.

00:07:07.403 --> 00:07:10.520
It's way better to have a physical copy

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.090
of your anxieties than it
is to keep it in your head.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.210
And try to be as thorough as possible.

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:18.450
Just doing that will help
you ease the burden off

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.640
of your subconscious.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.640
You're kinda just emptying your mind

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.010
onto a piece of paper.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.920
You're just clearing it of all the filth

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.670
and just putting it somewhere
that's outside of you.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.900
Now as constructive and relieving

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.920
as that will inevitably be,

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.430
I'd highly recommend
taking it a step further

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.390
and then organizing your tasks

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.860
according to the Eisenhower complex.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.430
Now the Eisenhower complex
is basically just a system

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.300
for organizing the importance

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.650
and urgency of your various tasks.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.960
Things that are both important and urgent,

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.120
you should do first,

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.080
things that are urgent
and not so important,

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.720
you should find a way to delegate

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.910
or do kind of a little bit later

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:57.920
or at the end of the day,

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.820
when you don't need as much mental energy.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.330
Things that are not urgent,

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.830
AK not time sensitive,
but are still important,

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.070
you should find a way
to plan for those things

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.860
and figure out a time where
you can slowly chip away at it

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.790
and things that are not
urgent and not important,

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.050
you just shouldn't do.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.450
Anything that's on your brain dump

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.800
that is neither urgent nor important,

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.860
you should find a way to just rid yourself

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.780
of the responsibility of doing that thing.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:25.750
I cannot express to you
how much mental clarity

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:26.680
this will give you.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.670
Just not having your
subconscious overloaded

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.100
with all of these tasks
and responsibilities

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.170
that you have to do

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.460
and instead have them present

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.570
on some sort of external
organized template

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.340
will free up your brain to work properly.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.130
Now, the third thing I wanna touch on

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:45.690
is something that's kind
of beaten like a dead horse

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.670
in the self-improvement community

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.220
but I have a few things to say about it.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.230
And that is mindfulness.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.820
Mindfulness is basically the
act of training your brain

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.720
to exist not in the
hypothetical, but in the real.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.460
You kind of bring your
consciousness from outside

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:06.940
of your head and all the
busy, anxious, noisy thoughts

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.740
that's going on in there inevitably

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.160
and you bring it into your body,

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.680
into what's in front of you,

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.840
what's tangible, the
sights, and the smells,

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.710
and the feelings all around you

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.500
and really stops you from
overthinking everything.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.180
And as we've kind of gone
over this overthinking

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:25.720
or hyper-cerebralization,

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:29.010
it is kind of the main
driver of brain fog.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.000
And one really interesting
thing about mindfulness

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.430
is that although it is best practice

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.320
to do it every single day,

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.690
you don't really have to.

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.030
Once you start learning the mechanics

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:43.380
of exiting your hyper-cerebralization

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.120
and entering the present moment,

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.790
you start to view the world
through a different lens,

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.390
a more objective lens.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:52.510
One that kind of accepts reality as it is.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.890
And this can change your
viewpoint permanently.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.810
If you find that you're someone
who overthinks everything,

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.120
you're prone to anxiety,
you're prone to overthinking,

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.430
mindfulness is kind of a no-brainer.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:04.890
So for like two weeks

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:08.110
just practice mindfulness
for five minutes a day,

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:11.940
there's a million tutorials on
YouTube as to how to do that.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.590
But I think it's kind of a no-brainer.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.410
So to recap, practice
graduated stimulation,

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.510
figure out what the most important things

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.480
that you need to do in the day are

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.130
and do those things first.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.560
Postpone your social media
binge as long as possible

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.420
and gradually ramp up
the entertainment value

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.660
of each activity that you
have to do as the day goes on.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.130
Secondly, practice brain dumping.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.850
Take everything that's
overloading your subconscious

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:40.690
and put it onto a physical media,

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.100
a giant word document
of every single thing

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.050
that you have to do.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.210
And then organize that brain dump

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.380
into the Eisenhower complex.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.650
Thirdly, practice mindfulness.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.690
Learn how to exit the noise off your head,

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:56.640
learn how to stop
hyper-cerebralizing everything

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.400
and enter the present moment

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.350
where things are a lot more
clear, simple, and calm.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.860
If you do these three things,

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:04.920
I would be shocked if
they didn't work for you

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.470
because these three things were some

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.985
of the most important things

00:11:07.985 --> 00:11:11.750
in giving me mental clarity
on a more consistent basis.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.570
And I really hope they
work for you as well.

